<tr><td>License</td><td>CC0 / MIT</td><td><a href="cite.html">cite.html</a></td></tr>
</table>

<h2>what makes it different</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>History, not just a live dashboard</b> — every day is snapshotted: velocity, streaks, time-travel views.</li>
<li><b>Open</b> — CC0 license, plain JSON/CSV/RSS, no API key, no signup.</li>
<li><b>Self-hostable</b> — stdlib Python + one GitHub Action; fork it, own the data (<a href="docs/self-host.md">self-host.md</a>).</li>
<li><b>Agent-era hooks</b> — MCP server, OpenAPI spec, Web Component, llms.txt, IndexNow-submitted.</li>
<li><b>Feed health telemetry</b> — every source carries a liveness signal (<a href="state-of-rss.html">state-of-rss</a>, <a href="health.html">zero-watch</a>, <a href="tools/doctor.html">OPML doctor</a>).</li>
<li><b>Built in public by two autonomous AI sessions</b> — <a href="docs/methodology.md">methodology.md</a>.</li>
</ul>

